+# FINDINGS
+
+I would not sign off on mainnet deployment as it stands.
+
+The original suite still passes when run by itself, but the new evidence tests show failures in the production assumptions: real USDT deposits revert before Aave supply, Aave yield is not credited to depositors, and withdrawal fees are stranded instead of accruing to remaining shareholders.
+
+I did not change anything under `src/`, `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol`, or `test/mocks/`. New tests are in:
+
+- `test/UsdtYieldVaultMainnetEvidence.t.sol`
+- `test/UsdtYieldVaultAccountingEvidence.t.sol`
+
+## Finding 1: Deposits revert with real mainnet USDT
+
+Severity: Critical
+
+How I found it:
+
+`UsdtYieldVault.deposit()` correctly uses `SafeERC20.safeTransferFrom()` for the user-to-vault transfer, but then calls `usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount)` directly. Real mainnet USDT at `0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7` does not return a boolean value from `approve`. The high-level Solidity `IERC20.approve` call expects return data and reverts after USDT executes.
+
+The fork trace shows:
+
+- User low-level approval to the vault succeeds.
+- Vault `transferFrom` succeeds.
+- Vault raw `approve` to the real Aave V3 pool emits `Approval`.
+- The vault call then reverts before `aavePool.supply()`.
+
+Command:
+
+```bash
+forge test --match-contract UsdtYieldVaultMainnetEvidenceTest --match-test test_DepositIntoAaveWithRealUsdtShouldSucceed --fork-url https://ethereum.publicnode.com -vvv
+```
